{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EtvTvaM6LSWSYnLQiUURxh","type":"tool_result","content":"===== qsa-53896.md section 4 =====\n## 4. MoE routing\n\n### Which layer implementation\n\n`vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py:160-171` — `class Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock(Qwen3NextSparseMoeBlock)`;\nits `__init__` only rejects sequence-parallel MoE and sets `n_shared_experts`, then\n`super().__init__(...)`. **[S]** Instantiated at `nvidia/model.py:245-247` when\n`num_experts > 0 and (layer_idx+1) % decoder_sparse_step == 0` (`:239-244`). **[S]**\n\nThe parent is stock vLLM: `vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_next.py:128` `class\nQwen3NextSparseMoeBlock(nn.Module)`, which builds `self.experts = FusedMoEFactory(... top_k=\nconfig.num_experts_per_tok, ...)` at `:215-235` and calls it at `:256-258`. **[S]** So: **vLLM\n`FusedMoE`, not `triton_kernels.matmul_ogs`, not a custom MoE.**\n\n### The routing code and the power-of-2 question\n\n`FusedMoEFactory` is defined at `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/layer.py:88` **[M]**.\nRouter selection lands in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/router_factory.py:230`\n`return FusedTopKRouter(...)` as the default fallback (`:76` comment: *\"7. FusedTopKRouter -\ndefault fallback\"*). **[S]**\n\n`FusedTopKRouter._compute_routing` — `router/fused_topk_router.py:156-174` — calls `fused_topk`\n(`:80-124`), which allocates `[M, topk]` tensors and dispatches to\n`vllm_topk_softmax` → `ops.topk_softmax` (`:33-42`) or `rocm_aiter_ops.topk_softmax` when\n`rocm_aiter_ops.is_fused_moe_enabled()` (`:64-69`, `:106-108`). **[S]**\n\n**There is no `tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)` and no power-of-2 requirement on this path.**\n`topk` is a plain runtime integer used only as a tensor dimension (`:92-103`). A\n`num_experts_per_tok = 10` routes fine.\n\n### Does the PR touch `triton_kernels` at all?\n\nNo. `grep -rln \"triton_kernels\" vllm/` returns 14 files, all mxfp4 / gpt-oss / aiter / quark /\nimport-util paths **[M]**; none of them is under `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/`. `find … -path\n\"*triton_kernels*\" -name \"*.py\"` inside the checkout returns only\n`vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py` and its test **[M]**\n— the third-party package itself is not vendored here.\n\nTwo further points that defuse the ds4-vllm concern for this PR:\n\n1. The evaluated checkpoint is **FP8**, not mxfp4:\n   `tests/evals/qwen4_exp/configs/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8.yaml` → `model_name:\n   \"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8\"`, `server_args: \"--tensor-parallel-size 4\"`; both\n   `configs/models-h200.txt` and `models-b200.txt` list only that yaml **[S]**. FP8 MoE goes\n   through `fused_moe/oracle/fp8.py` (`select_fp8_moe_backend` at `:305`, ROCm/CUDA branch at\n   `:447`), which resolves to `TritonExperts` (`:190-194`) or `rocm_aiter_moe` (`:204`) — not the\n   gpt-oss triton_kernels path.\n2. Even if it did land there, **this branch already carries the pow2 fix**:\n   `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py:209-224`\n   `_patch_legacy_routing_for_nonpow2_topk()`, whose docstring names the exact defect —\n   *\"The bundled `_routing_compute_indx` does `tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)`, which fails\n   to compile when `N_EXPTS_ACT` (top_k) is not a power of 2 (6 * 32 = 192)\"* — and installs\n   `_routing_compute_indx_pow2` with `BLOCK_SIZE_PADDED` (`:239-270`, note `local_offs =\n   tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE_PADDED)` at `:260` and `BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr = N_EXPTS_ACT *\n   BLOCK_M` at `:259`, with masking at `:262-266`). **[S]** The fix the ds4-vllm campaign called\n   mandatory is already upstream in this tree.\n\n### The ROCm (non-CUDA) build's exact path\n\n`Qwen4ExpForCausalLM` from `amd/model.py` (dispatch in §3) → `Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock`\n(`amd/model.py:245-247`, the file is a mirror of nvidia's — `amd/model.py:239-247` matches\n`nvidia/model.py:239-247` by grep **[M]**) → `Qwen3NextSparseMoeBlock` → `FusedMoEFactory` →\n`FusedTopKRouter` → `fused_topk` → **`rocm_aiter_ops.topk_softmax` if\n`rocm_aiter_ops.is_fused_moe_enabled()` else `ops.topk_softmax`**\n(`router/fused_topk_router.py:64-69`, `:106-111`) → experts kernel from `oracle/fp8.py`\n(`rocm_aiter_moe` at `:204`, with an aiter skip predicate at `:409-414` falling back to\n`TritonExperts`). **No triton_kernels, no `N_EXPTS_ACT`.** **[S]**\n\n## 5. The QSA tests — what they assert, and what they cannot catch","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1182cd30-62fd-41c8-9446-e16b11d402f2","uuid":"b65ddf89-e53b-40f6-bacc-7d8a1ffbd7cd","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:14:08.474Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== qsa-53896.md section 4 =====\n## 4. MoE routing\n\n### Which layer implementation\n\n`vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py:160-171` — `class Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock(Qwen3NextSparseMoeBlock)`;\nits `__init__` only rejects sequence-parallel MoE and sets `n_shared_experts`, then\n`super().__init__(...)`. **[S]** Instantiated at `nvidia/model.py:245-247` when\n`num_experts > 0 and (layer_idx+1) % decoder_sparse_step == 0` (`:239-244`). **[S]**\n\nThe parent is stock vLLM: `vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_next.py:128` `class\nQwen3NextSparseMoeBlock(nn.Module)`, which builds `self.experts = FusedMoEFactory(... top_k=\nconfig.num_experts_per_tok, ...)` at `:215-235` and calls it at `:256-258`. **[S]** So: **vLLM\n`FusedMoE`, not `triton_kernels.matmul_ogs`, not a custom MoE.**\n\n### The routing code and the power-of-2 question\n\n`FusedMoEFactory` is defined at `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/layer.py:88` **[M]**.\nRouter selection lands in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/router_factory.py:230`\n`return FusedTopKRouter(...)` as the default fallback (`:76` comment: *\"7. FusedTopKRouter -\ndefault fallback\"*). **[S]**\n\n`FusedTopKRouter._compute_routing` — `router/fused_topk_router.py:156-174` — calls `fused_topk`\n(`:80-124`), which allocates `[M, topk]` tensors and dispatches to\n`vllm_topk_softmax` → `ops.topk_softmax` (`:33-42`) or `rocm_aiter_ops.topk_softmax` when\n`rocm_aiter_ops.is_fused_moe_enabled()` (`:64-69`, `:106-108`). **[S]**\n\n**There is no `tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)` and no power-of-2 requirement on this path.**\n`topk` is a plain runtime integer used only as a tensor dimension (`:92-103`). A\n`num_experts_per_tok = 10` routes fine.\n\n### Does the PR touch `triton_kernels` at all?\n\nNo. `grep -rln \"triton_kernels\" vllm/` returns 14 files, all mxfp4 / gpt-oss / aiter / quark /\nimport-util paths **[M]**; none of them is under `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/`. `find … -path\n\"*triton_kernels*\" -name \"*.py\"` inside the checkout returns only\n`vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py` and its test **[M]**\n— the third-party package itself is not vendored here.\n\nTwo further points that defuse the ds4-vllm concern for this PR:\n\n1. The evaluated checkpoint is **FP8**, not mxfp4:\n   `tests/evals/qwen4_exp/configs/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8.yaml` → `model_name:\n   \"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8\"`, `server_args: \"--tensor-parallel-size 4\"`; both\n   `configs/models-h200.txt` and `models-b200.txt` list only that yaml **[S]**. FP8 MoE goes\n   through `fused_moe/oracle/fp8.py` (`select_fp8_moe_backend` at `:305`, ROCm/CUDA branch at\n   `:447`), which resolves to `TritonExperts` (`:190-194`) or `rocm_aiter_moe` (`:204`) — not the\n   gpt-oss triton_kernels path.\n2. Even if it did land there, **this branch already carries the pow2 fix**:\n   `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py:209-224`\n   `_patch_legacy_routing_for_nonpow2_topk()`, whose docstring names the exact defect —\n   *\"The bundled `_routing_compute_indx` does `tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)`, which fails\n   to compile when `N_EXPTS_ACT` (top_k) is not a power of 2 (6 * 32 = 192)\"* — and installs\n   `_routing_compute_indx_pow2` with `BLOCK_SIZE_PADDED` (`:239-270`, note `local_offs =\n   tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE_PADDED)` at `:260` and `BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr = N_EXPTS_ACT *\n   BLOCK_M` at `:259`, with masking at `:262-266`). **[S]** The fix the ds4-vllm campaign called\n   mandatory is already upstream in this tree.\n\n### The ROCm (non-CUDA) build's exact path\n\n`Qwen4ExpForCausalLM` from `amd/model.py` (dispatch in §3) → `Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock`\n(`amd/model.py:245-247`, the file is a mirror of nvidia's — `amd/model.py:239-247` matches\n`nvidia/model.py:239-247` by grep **[M]**) → `Qwen3NextSparseMoeBlock` → `FusedMoEFactory` →\n`FusedTopKRouter` → `fused_topk` → **`rocm_aiter_ops.topk_softmax` if\n`rocm_aiter_ops.is_fused_moe_enabled()` else `ops.topk_softmax`**\n(`router/fused_topk_router.py:64-69`, `:106-111`) → experts kernel from `oracle/fp8.py`\n(`rocm_aiter_moe` at `:204`, with an aiter skip predicate at `:409-414` falling back to\n`TritonExperts`). **No triton_kernels, no `N_EXPTS_ACT`.** **[S]**\n\n## 5. The QSA tests — what they assert, and what they cannot catch","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
