test_instruments.py\"],\"taskId\":\"instruments\"},\"pullRequest\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f\",\"regated\":false,\"taskId\":\"instruments\",\"trailer\":null}\nhandoff/harvest-2026-08-29/capture/01a04d1e-4f48-7091-a788-aeb19cd24627.out:1:TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={\"baseRevision\":\"71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa\",\"blocked\":[{\"blockedBy\":[\"proxy-tooling\"],\"taskId\":\"proxy-tooling\"},{\"blockedBy\":[\"morning-ledger\"],\"taskId\":\"morning-ledger\"},{\"blockedBy\":[\"catalog-handoff\"],\"taskId\":\"catalog-handoff\"},{\"blockedBy\":[\"proxy-tooling\"],\"taskId\":\"cp-proxy\"},{\"blockedBy\":[\"proxy-tooling\"],\"taskId\":\"cp-tp2\"},{\"blockedBy\":[\"proxy-tooling\"],\"taskId\":\"cp-bench\"},{\"blockedBy\":[\"proxy-tooling\",\"morning-ledger\",\"catalog-handoff\"],\"taskId\":\"cp-close\"}],\"campaign\":\"flashnext\",\"checkpoints\":[],\"closingSummary\":null,\"complete\":false,\"deferrals\":[{\"taskId\":\"cp-weights\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]},{\"taskId\":\"cp-build\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]},{\"taskId\":\"cp-smoke\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]},{\"taskId\":\"cp-proxy\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]},{\"taskId\":\"cp-tp2\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]},{\"taskId\":\"cp-bench\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]},{\"taskId\":\"cp-close\",\"waitingOn\":[\"rdma-package\"]}],\"diagnoses\":[{\"attempt\":1,\"comment\":\"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/11\",\"diagnosis\":\"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains because attempt 1 ended with an empty lane: the worktree is clean, HEAD is still the prepared base 71f2beb, the captured diff is empty, and the driver reported \\\"agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\\\" (the accompanying result-projection-timeout is a downstream symptom of the worker exiting without a final projected result, not the cause). Neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh exists on disk, so no partial work is recoverable and attempt 2 must author both files from scratch. Steering for attempt 2: (1) Write scripts/make-proxy.sh in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh; it runs inside the container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy (same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128x128, small lookup table with the shard tensor name the mmap path expects), reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout rather than inventing generators, and making the build idempotent — steering says the checkpoint at /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy and the flashnext:dev image already exist, so detect and reuse rather than rebuild. (2) Write scripts/run-proxy.sh to serve single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, request one greedy completion, assert finite logits via the API, shut down cleanly, and write results/receipts/proxy.json at runtime; the literal string results/receipts/proxy.json must appear in the script for the acceptance argv grep. (3) Apply the ratified serve fix: pass --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling and do not chase the OOM via VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, which the later overseer correction superseded (the host logs integrated_gpu=False). Optionally export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True. Record the flag choice in the script and in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. (4) Ownership discipline, which is what killed attempt 1: run the acceptance argv and see it pass, then git add ONLY paths inside the binding write boundary scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/, then git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message. (5) Correction to steering comment 7: results/receipts/proxy.json is NOT inside this task's conflictDomains and must not be staged or committed — committing it would fail conflict-domains on attempt 2 exactly as an empty lane failed it on attempt 1. The receipt is produced at runtime by run-proxy.sh and left untracked; if it appears in git status, leave it unstaged is not sufficient because the porcelain check must be clean, so have run-proxy.sh write it only when executed, not during the commit sequence, and verify the untracked receipt is absent from the lane before committing. Any test coverage for the two scripts belongs under tests/.\",\"taskId\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"verdict\":\"retry\"},{\"attempt\":2,\"comment\":\"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/12\",\"diagnosis\":\"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains a second time with an empty lane, and the two-attempt cap is now exhausted: HEAD is still the prepared base 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, `git status --porcelain` (including ignored) is empty, the captured patch is empty, neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh exists on disk, and no artifact of the attempt survives anywhere in the worktree. The driver's `agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base` is the operative failure; the accompanying result-schema-mismatch / result-projection-timeout (finalMessage not projected within 10000 ms, exitEvidencePassed false) is the downstream symptom of the worker exiting without a projected final result, identical in shape to attempt 1, so it is a reproducible task-shape failure rather than a one-off machinery fault and does not warrant spending machinery-retry budget. Attempt 1's retry steering already told the worker exactly what to author and to commit before returning; repeating it a third time is not available and, on the evidence, would not change the outcome. The out-of-task cause that blocks this lane is a contradiction between the task's own deliverables and its binding write boundary: the goal requires run-proxy.sh to write results/receipts/proxy.json and deliveredBehaviors require the first light actually to execute on the GPU, but results/receipts/ is outside conflictDomains [redacted-token] and is not gitignored, so executing the script deposits an untracked results/receipts/proxy.json in the lane that can neither be committed (it would fail conflict-domains) nor left behind (it dirties the worktree the ownership stage validates). Authorized steering comment 7 compounds this by explicitly instructing the worker to `git add` results/receipts/proxy.json — following ratified steering would itself trip conflict-domains. The sibling precedent confirms the grant is the operator's to make: container-recipe committed results/receipts/build.json in c1363cb, and scripts/run-smoke.sh (the cited style reference) writes results/receipts/smoke.json into the repo the same way. Additionally, the authoring work that the single acceptance criterion checks (bash -n plus a grep for the receipt path) is cheap, while the goal drags in a full container build, synthetic-checkpoint construction under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy, and a live single-node serve with first-light assertions; that live execution is what consumes the worker session before it commits, and it belongs to the cp-proxy checkpoint, not to this implementation task. The serve-side technical questions are already settled and need no further investigation: pass --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes, keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6, do not use --skip-mm-profiling, and disregard the superseded VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY steer since the host logs integrated_gpu=False. Operator action: grant results/receipts/proxy.json to this task's write boundary and re-scope the task to authoring plus committing the two scripts, leaving the live first light to cp-proxy.\",\"proposal\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.\",\"id\":\"proxy-scripts-clean\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.\",\"id\":\"proxy-serve-flags\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh\"],\"description\":\"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.\",\"id\":\"proxy-checkpoint-layout\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"[ -z \\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\" ]\"],\"description\":\"The lane is fully committed: no uncommitted or untracked files remain after the task's commit.\",\"id\":\"proxy-lane-clean\"}],\"dependencies\":[\"container-recipe\"],\"goal\":\"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\"kind\":\"amendment-task\",\"paths\":[\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\",\"results/receipts/proxy.json\"]},\"taskId\":\"proxy-tooling\",\"verdict\":\"blocked\"},{\"attempt\":1,\"comment\":\"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/15\",\"diagnosis\":\"Aborted in the lane stage before any worktree was prepared, so no worker ever ran and no task content was implicated. The recorded failure is a flow-error whose detail is the harness exception FlowAdmissionDenied (code admission-denied, ordinal 4, at line 3377 column 25) with an empty details object; exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, meaning no command was executed and no gate ran. gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason 'task failed before a worktree was prepared' at base rev all-zeros. Nothing in the task morning-ledger points at the failure: the sole acceptance criterion ledger-sections is a plain grep over docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the authorized docs conflict domain, and it was never evaluated. The dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are also not implicated, because dependency resolution would surface as a task-level block rather than an admission denial raised inside the flow engine itself. Admission denial at lane entry with no stderr, no exit code, and no worktree is a scheduler/session fault in the machinery that admits lanes, not an authorable defect in the repository and not a gate-contract or authority problem the operator must grant. The correct disposition is therefore to charge the bounded machinery-retry budget and re-admit the lane unchanged; if admission is denied again at the same ordinal, the fault is durable in the flow layer and should be escalated to the operator rather than retried further.\",\"taskId\":\"morning-ledger\",\"verdict\":\"blocked\"},{\"attempt\":1,\"comment\":\"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/18\",\"diagnosis\":\"Failed at lane admission before any worktree, worker invocation, or gate execution occurred, so no task-content defect is implicated. Evidence: the failure stage is `lane` with verdict `flow-error` and detail `FlowAdmissionDenied` / code `admission-denied` (ordinal 4, empty details), exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason \\\"task failed before a worktree was prepared\\\". Because the flow controller refused to admit the lane, the worker never read specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5 and never created handoff/catalog-row.patch or handoff/README.md; the sole acceptance criterion catalog-patch-wellformed was never evaluated, and there is no failing check id or offending path to cite. Nothing in the task is at fault: it is an implementation task with no dependencies, a single conflict domain of \\\"handoff\\\" that is also its only authorized write prefix, and no needs-authority envelope was returned. There is likewise no out-of-task cause to name — no missing authority, no gate-contract defect, no upstream source fix, since the denial carries no adjudicable reason payload and no work product exists to attribute it to. This is a scheduler/session-level admission fault in the campaign machinery (for example lane-slot or conflict-domain admission contention on \\\"handoff\\\"), which is precisely what the bounded machinery-retry budget covers; a re-admission of the identical lane at revision sha256:3a04f0fc89c3e88303af3a5b38fc8a4bd52f2f81715bfecfc42bdc04ba5c2269 is the correct next action. If admission is denied again with the same code and still-empty details, the recurrence stops being incidental and should be escalated to the operator as a flow-configuration problem rather than continuing to consume retries.\",\"taskId\":\"catalog-handoff\",\"verdict\":\"blocked\"}],\"escalation\":null,\"frontier\":[{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -q '503c5ae1e72aa9ed91925dafa3d82ee2e992747f' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -q '76ba39b630a70accb72f19388eefe48844b50eb8' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && ! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*(sudo[[:space:]]+)?(insmod|modprobe)[[:space:]]' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -qi 'physically present' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'worker first' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'deploy' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && test -s host/rdma/ab-protocol.md\"],\"description\":\"Scripts syntax-clean, pins present, no auto-install, attended language present.\",\"id\":\"rdma-package-sound\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"host/rdma\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"Tomorrow's attended RDMA bring-up is one script plus one checklist plus one adoption gate\",\"No unsigned module can load unattended from anything this repo ships\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"The bootstrap session scoped an operator-attended RDMA bring-up package (spec ruling P7, claim 6.4 — specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6): host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh (pinned out-of-tree module fetch, kernel-version and secure-boot guards, staged install only), host/rdma/attended-bringup.md (the coordinated-reboot checklist with the port-controller recovery path), host/rdma/ab-protocol.md (the socket-versus-verbs adoption gate). If those files already exist in the tree, verify them against the reference bring-up doctrine in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 7 plus specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-hardening-addendum.md and fix defects; if absent, author them from those sections' pins. Hard rules: nothing GPL is vendored — the two out-of-tree repositories are fetched at their pinned commits by the script; nothing installs or loads automatically; one rail only; the checklist states plainly that bring-up happens with the operator physically present, starts only after a committed socket-transport benchmark exists under results/, opens with the worker deploy-path repoint off the fast rail, and orders reboots worker first, never both at once. Extend the tests suite so the syntax sweep covers host/rdma and a test asserts the two pin commits appear in fetch-and-build.sh. Boundaries: touch only host/rdma and tests/.\",\"id\":\"rdma-package\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/stage-weights.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:b322b54d6da9831c25a2e55569a9a8ce4c293840285b6225b2760d2c20ee9460\",\"title\":\"Integrate the operator-attended RDMA package under host/rdma\"}],\"inputEpochs\":{\"bench-harness\":\"sha256:2352e45654aa40b953261c40e9f6ec94f1092cad33d430f9ecf48e6f10e3c5eb\",\"catalog-handoff\":\"sha256:94d761662378a9c6a78bb5f60b9cd6cfbc89e56419945e15d63b493ed994f4e9\",\"container-recipe\":\"sha256:597bcbb9ee96cc98997c446dcd92c490489300e35163a5d59b7037f6030d6758\",\"cp-bench\":\"sha256:b664febb5bb3a52e84267bd7c4f343753c56be5d98796fc517cc6a565847b003\",\"cp-build\":\"sha256:2a39e30082d563c7b5088199b5da6df98513e32d371d384e9c33f8d8f5a6a629\",\"cp-close\":\"sha256:d0561387144934af0071a18388de11968a5dd96ba199ce6599b35b46905fa14e\",\"cp-proxy\":\"sha256:a3d50f72301ae0c33b0b2aa0e8b8533dc139372f2f06ccfefd10b33dc9fbf05c\",\"cp-smoke\":\"sha256:5678368f6a54d9797cbd69e04644d2f3d542b92653c8fc00d1b0881d4cb76ecb\",\"cp-tp2\":\"sha256:6bb34cc2a74aca9267004f096723ac202a9715290bbf3b51c05b9e55aa5c91e9\",\"cp-weights\":\"sha256:7e1479062d9c8f01724cea119dd68290d90e6501b7c3b6d232f254f082013990\",\"host-tooling\":\"sha256:b771d06ffbc5cd093ade0388dbf7dd8d390243cf5e3a7e92dce2bedb4b78a0ff\",\"instruments\":\"sha256:347517ad56e50308317a8a6db7e931c56d2b850afeec55dbaa2f514bb01b333c\",\"morning-ledger\":\"sha256:5299ae20113a6c75b529f2e56d080294e9b3ee2931ba72466d381b49dafa1747\",\"proxy-tooling\":\"sha256:5be1f56071505ef1d573b0d5e4c8edffac379fdad097495bfb579a4f38cef9c1\",\"rdma-package\":\"sha256:7362f764d07dfb573ee2a7f3bece7b6b4fa5d7173e0e6b23d0f7f5b9ed9d8e2a\"},\"merged\":[{\"mergeCommit\":\"c1363cb2308e16f3d96bd92e8cde7c94261d4cb9\",\"pullRequest\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/tally/flashnext-campaign-01