{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYCvXDxbSxEptbwLduMM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Reconcile complete — the deliverable is already in the lane, verified end to end\n\n**Acceptance criteria: pass.**\n\n```\npython3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_{synctrace,offload_batch,expert_union}.py\ngrep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l  →  3\npython3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v  →  Ran 11 tests ... OK\n```\n\nFull repo suite also green: 50 tests across all five test modules.\n\nI did not take the prior attempt's word for it — I re-read both cited spec sections and all four files, and checked the deliverable against the *goal*, not just the acceptance command:\n\n- **`container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py`** — wraps the seven `torch.Tensor` methods that force a blocking D2H (`item/tolist/cpu/numpy/nonzero/__float__/__int__`), one `sys._getframe(1)` per call, and carries upstream's bool-mask-indexing caveat verbatim (ds4-vllm-manifest §3.1). No env of its own; `install()`/`uninstall()` bracket the `FN_PROFILE` window — matching the reference's deliberate no-new-env-var discipline.\n- **`container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py`** — `resolve_store_batch_tokens` / `resolve_promote_block_budget` on `FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC` / `FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC`, torch-free (`import os` only), with both load-bearing invariants intact: store floor at `max(offloaded_block_sizes)`, promotion counted in blocks not tokens (§3.3).\n- **`container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py`** — correctly **re-targeted** as the goal requires: wraps `fused_topk` in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py`, not upstream's `gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data`, which this FP8 Qwen4Exp path never reaches (qsa-53896 §4: `FusedMoEFactory → FusedTopKRouter → fused_topk`). Kill switch `FN_EXPERT_UNION` defaults off; `FN_EU_START/CALLS/OUT` shape the window; device-only accumulation with slot-0 padding absorption, single `.cpu()` at flush.\n- **`tests/test_instruments.py`** — asserts all three required things plus the `DS4_`→`FN_` rename and that no bytecode is *tracked* in the overlay.\n\nAll three carry an `Adapted from` notice naming the upstream file, revision `a8f620d`, and Apache License 2.0. The overlay ships via `container/Containerfile:117`.\n\n**No code change made.** The three modules and the test are byte-identical to their landing commit `4b1d714`, which is an ancestor of the lane base `ff1731c`; re-authoring identical files produces no diff, only history churn. The tree is clean and this task's work — plus `43eb34b`, the reconcile record already in the lane — is committed on `tally-work/flashnext-e55ddef1f9e3/instruments`. `git status --porcelain` prints nothing.\n\nOne thing worth flagging, outside my write boundary: there is no in-repo `FN_PROFILE` driver or `install()` call site for `fn_synctrace`/`fn_expert_union` — those live engine-side in the fork patch, which belongs to the container-recipe domain, not `container/rootfs` or `tests`. The modules are correct and importable as specified; wiring them to a call site is a different task's surface."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":555,"cache_read_input_tokens":57356,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":555},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1182cd30-62fd-41c8-9446-e16b11d402f2","uuid":"4c7df418-e966-4bf6-a766-a6c6e6d5f19e","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:16:00.443Z","request_id":"req_011CeYCvWPrRQYshkrWWg15n"}
